From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 14:46:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 11305/11362] Resolve the eval-run corpus from the main
 checkout inside a worktree (REQ-ARC-WMTE-6642)

The pre-commit hook eval-run-consumer-field-lint refused every scripts/*.py
commit made from a git worktree or a fresh clone. The corpus
results/arc_leaderboard_eval_runs/ is gitignored, so a worktree has none,
and the lint failed closed on the missing directory. Reproduced in this
worktree before the change, directly and through pre-commit:

  FAIL: runs directory missing, join cannot run: <worktree>/results/arc_leaderboard_eval_runs
  hook id: eval-run-consumer-field-lint, exit code: 1

The lint's own test_real_repo_contract_holds was RED in the worktree for
the same reason (1 failed, 6 passed, carnot imported from the worktree).

What changed. With no --runs-dir the corpus now resolves in order: this
checkout, then the main checkout found through git rev-parse
--git-common-dir, then none. A directory counts only when it holds an
artifact, so a bare mkdir is not a corpus. With none, the artifact half of
the join is SKIPPED and the skip is printed on its own NOTE line and on the
final OK line. An explicit --runs-dir that is missing or empty still fails.

Fail direction, decided and written in the docstring. FAIL CLOSED on
everything that means the lint could not look: no scripts/ or python/ tree
(new), an empty producer surface (new), an unparseable consumer, an explicit
missing corpus. The corpus itself is a pass-widener: an artifact key can only
turn a failure into a pass, so with the corpus absent every declared field
must be wired in producer source and the failures are a superset of the full
join's (test_missing_corpus_never_admits_more). The skip costs precision in
the loud direction, never safety.

Rejected. Passing an absolute --runs-dir from the hook: a hardcoded write
target that breaks every other machine. Failing closed on a missing corpus
as before: it refused legitimate work in the dominant workflow with no gain
on the fail side, and the friction pushes people to bypass hooks.

Measured on the live checkout: 7 consumers, 190 producer files, 15
artifacts, 476 keys with the main corpus; 20 declared fields pass on
producer source alone, 0 fail.

Proof. 13 mutations at the call sites, 13 RED, byte-identical restores by
cmp, final GREEN. One survivor (the bare-repository check) was pinned with a
named test and re-run RED. Ran UNLOCKED: --mutation-begin refuses a
worktree. PYTHONPATH pinned to this worktree and the imported carnot path
printed before every run.

Step 6: the check IS the fix. The hook now passes from this worktree and
names the main corpus it used.

